From 0645f4a08106caad9084936d39b69ac1a04b1bcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venkatesh <inventvenkat@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Jul 2025 18:01:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(connector): [WORLDPAY] Handle text/html 404 responses
 gracefully
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Worldpay returns 404 errors with text/html content type instead of JSON for PSync requests. This causes deserialization failures that get mapped to 5xx errors. This fix:

1. Adds a reusable utility function `is_html_response_from_headers` to check Content-Type headers
2. Uses this utility in Worldpay error handlers to detect HTML responses
3. Returns proper 4xx errors for HTML responses instead of attempting JSON deserialization

Fixes #8748

